      "challenges": [
        {
          "finding": "Weak alert reporting, and weak listing and follow-up of contacts around confirmed cases.",
          "source_section": "1.2 Epidemiological surveillance",
          "topic": "weak_alert_reporting"
        },
        {
          "finding": "Insufficient operationalisation of points of entry and control: functionality remains weak in Tshopo with only 6 of 19 (32%) activated and reporting completeness limited to 57%. Performance is further affected by screening refusals (2,100 people, 2.9%, in Nord-Kivu), assaults on providers and non-observance of the health protocol by some authorities at the Mukulia control point; a further 48 screening refusals (1.2%) were recorded, motivated by denial of the disease and fear of being admitted to a treatment centre.",
          "source_section": "1.3 Points of entry and control",
          "topic": "poe_coverage_gap"
        },
        {
          "finding": "Insufficient referral capacity (2 ambulances out of service in Ituri, no ambulance in 7 Nord-Kivu health zones and no treatment centre in 4) and saturation of several treatment centres. In Haut-Uele no standard-compliant treatment centre exists across the 6 affected health zones, and mobility for burial teams is insufficient in the Wamba area.",
          "source_section": "1.6 Continuity of care",
          "topic": "ambulance_shortage"
        },
        {
          "finding": "Persistent community challenges: an announced strike by the psychosocial pillar and demotivation from non-payment in Nord-Kivu, removal of a positive body by the community to a family cemetery in Katwa, refusal of safe and dignified burials (10 failures at Mangala and 4 at Komanda in Ituri) and refusal of sampling in Tshopo, liable to affect community adherence to the response.",
          "source_section": "1.7 Risk communication and community engagement",
          "topic": "community_adherence_risk"
        },
        {
          "finding": "Persistent logistical needs to support the expansion of the response, notably completion of the treatment-centre extensions, continuous supply of essential inputs and PPE, and availability of transport and evacuation means.",
          "source_section": "1.8 Logistics",
          "topic": "resource_gap"
        },
        {
          "finding": "Persistent insecurity, incidents involving local authorities and community resistance during safe and dignified burials: physical assaults on providers and on law-enforcement personnel at the Mukulia control point, and insecurity plus a stockout of protective suits blocking 10 burials at Mangala.",
          "source_section": "1.9 Security",
          "topic": "insecurity_access"
        },
        {
          "finding": "Still insufficient coverage of awareness activities and of the prevention, reporting and case-management mechanisms for sexual exploitation and abuse across the zones concerned by the response.",
          "source_section": "1.10 Protection from sexual exploitation and abuse",
          "topic": "psea_coverage_gap"
        }
      ],
